<section class="content-section product-detail-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">BUYER'S GUIDE</p><h2>What to evaluate in restaurant POS software</h2><p>Restaurant POS software sits at the centre of day-to-day service. Before choosing a system, map how your team handles billing, order changes, payment methods, kitchen communication, end-of-day reconciliation and reports. Confirm which of these workflows Vyfoo supports for your restaurant and hardware.</p></div><div class="page-grid"><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">01</span><h3>Service and billing flow</h3><p>Document how orders are entered, modified, billed and closed, including refunds or cancellations that staff may need to handle.</p></article>
<article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">02</span><h3>Hardware and connectivity</h3><p>Confirm supported devices, printers, network requirements, backup procedures and the way the restaurant operates during an outage.</p></article>
<article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">03</span><h3>Reporting and operating controls</h3><p>Identify which sales summaries, user permissions and reconciliation tasks are necessary, then check these against the product's confirmed scope.</p></article></div></div></section>
